# Old-vs-new byte comparison of t4a_cuda_reduce / t4a_cuda_reduce_any (strategy PLANE).
# A100 80GB PCIe, driver 580.178.04, CUDA 12.6 (V12.6.85). Cubins:
#   old.cubin    = nvcc -std=c++17 -cubin -arch=sm_80 -I cuda/include  ab7395c:cuda/src/reduce.cu
#   new.cubin    = the same on this branch's cuda/src/reduce.cu
#   mutant.cubin = this branch with the steady-state batch folded in reverse (all ops);
#   mutant-extrema.cubin = the same for MAX/MIN only
#                  (`for (int b = B - 1; b >= 0; --b)` in the second fold loop): the fail path.
# $ g++ -O2 -std=c++17 -I/usr/local/cuda-12.6/include combine-old-vs-new.cpp \
#       -L/usr/local/cuda-12.6/lib64/stubs -lcuda -o combine-old-vs-new
# $ ./combine-old-vs-new old.cubin new.cubin   (then old/old, old/mutant, old/mutant-extrema)
# Per route: 15 geometries x 3 layouts (axis-major, strided, reversed) x 2 entries x 48 outputs.
# Exit 0: all compared, no value/nanness difference; 1: a value/nanness difference; 2: CUDA
# failure or incomplete comparison. "payload-only" = both NaN, different bits (outside the ABI
# Payload differences are tolerated only on F64/C64 SUM/PROD/SUM_SQUARES; elsewhere they count as payload-violation (a failure). Counts are outputs.
